    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d723">

                <pb facs="1449" n="1437" sameAs="frus:frus1946v09/pg1437"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">Marshall Mission Files, Lot 54–D270:
                    Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">General Marshall to
                        Mr. Walter S. Robertson, at
                    Peiping</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Nanking</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1946-08-01">1 August 1946</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1224. Reference your 6268,<anchor n="24" xml:id="d723-f1"/> since Nationalist and
                    Communists both wish to make a factfinding investigation, it appears advisable
                    to send a special team carefully selected especially as to American member.</p>
                <p>General Chou En Lai concurs in this message.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
